{%- comment -%}
  Tidy money for display (never changes a value):
    • drops the decimals on a whole amount (£120.00 → £120; keeps £19.99)
    • hides the ISO code for unambiguous symbols (£ GBP, € EUR), keeps it for
      shared ones ($ = USD / AUD / …):  $108.00 USD → $108 USD

  Rendered SERVER-SIDE, so the price is correct on first paint and on every section
  re-render (variant change, cart update) — there is no client-side catch-up, so it
  cannot flash. Mirrors assets/wb-price-format.js, which does the same to any price
  not routed through here (unit price, cart line items, etc.).

  Accepts:
    amount — price in cents (integer). Presentment currency is applied by the `money`
             filter automatically under Shopify Markets.
    code   — pass `code: false` to never append the ISO code (used for the per-unit
             price, where the main price already carries the currency).

  Assumes a prefix currency symbol (every WB market is £/$). A suffix-symbol currency
  would simply keep its .00 — untidied, never wrong.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign wb_m = amount | money
  # Guard against a nil/blank amount (e.g. an absent compare-at price) so we never
  # emit a lone currency code.
  if wb_m != blank
    assign wb_last3 = wb_m | slice: -3, 3
    if wb_last3 == '.00' or wb_last3 == ',00'
      assign wb_cut = wb_m | size | minus: 3
      assign wb_m = wb_m | slice: 0, wb_cut
    endif
    unless code == false
      assign wb_iso = cart.currency.iso_code | default: shop.currency
      assign wb_hide_codes = 'GBP,EUR' | split: ','
      unless wb_hide_codes contains wb_iso
        assign wb_m = wb_m | append: ' ' | append: wb_iso
      endunless
    endunless
  endif
  echo wb_m
-%}
